// ownerview/test.php - the PHP half of the ownerview suite (2026-10-01).
//
// Lifts the editor-role decisions out of the files under test by stable text
// anchors (anchors that exist in the pre-change build too, so the control shows
// real RED rows rather than a FATAL) and evals them over a role matrix with the
// grant / owner / authorization helpers stubbed. Nothing is included, no
// database is opened.
//
//   index.php      the role block ($canEditLoadedReport, $canScheduleLoadedReport,
//                  $admin_class), the owner promotion + the view gate, the
//                  journal block ($pnbJrnAccess = manage_journal.php's own gate,
//                  $pnbJrnWanted), the status bar's role badges ($sb_is_owner)
//                  and the role-pill markup itself
//   dashboard.php  $mayView / $canEdit
//   query.php      $penumbraCanAuthorReport (guardrail copy) and the view check
//   static         the console + penumbra_vars still key on the editor flag, the
//                  ?asof= gate follows the promotion, journalAccess reaches
//                  penumbra_vars, the copy and the help text
//   help render    help_content.php rendered for a non-admin and an admin: the
//                  View Options and Report Journal topics reach both
//
// usage: php -n test.php <dir holding index.php dashboard.php query.php
//                          help_content.php main.js>
// Prints one line per assertion:  A|<id>|<1 pass, 0 fail>|<name>|<detail>
// then "<n> assertions, <m> failed", or FATAL|<why> when an anchor is gone.
// =============================================================================
